menu "Protected mode demo"

config UMODE_ONCHIP_USER_KB
    int "On-chip memory granted to U-mode (KiB)"
    default 192
    range 64 320
    help
        How much of the internal SRAM belongs to the user side.

        The kernel keeps everything else.  This is the whole of the on-chip
        split: the PMP grants U-mode read and write over exactly this pool and
        over PSRAM, and nothing else, so every other byte of internal memory --
        the kernel's heap, its stacks, its data -- is unreachable from U-mode
        by hardware rather than by a check the kernel makes.

        The user arenas are carved out of this pool, so it must hold at least
        USER_SLOTS * USER_ARENA_SIZE with room to spare.

        It is a static array, so raising it takes internal RAM away from the
        kernel one for one, and the build fails if it will not fit.

endmenu
